<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Greco-Turkish War (1897)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1897">1897</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Thirty Days' War</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greco-turkish-war-1919-1922">Greco-Turkish War</a> of 1897, also called the Thirty Days' War, was fought between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a> over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crete">Crete</a>, where Christians had risen against Ottoman rule. Ottoman forces defeated the Greek army in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thessaly">Thessaly</a> within weeks. Greece paid an indemnity and accepted international financial control, but the great powers then forced the Ottomans to grant Crete autonomy.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/greco-turkish-war-1897.jpg" alt="Greco-Turkish War (1897)" width="320" height="206" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Fausto Zonaro · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:D%C3%B6meke_Harbi_Zonaro.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
